  "body": "## New result\n\nThis adds **constructive chronological attainment**, not a new lower bound. Ali Romman's #1125 already proves the asynchronous 32-path obstruction and explicitly does not construct a schedule at 32 paths (its PROOF lines 204\u2013206). For the exact eight-centre P104 fixture from Josie Elliston's #1071, the new certificate executes all **416 reads on 104 targets in 32 monotone fixed-centre chains**, attaining that existing bound. The additional array count is **24 rather than #1071's 47** under a global centre order.\n\n- 116 source-bound prefix edges specify independent target read orders.\n- Explicit chain assignments plus increasing-frame-dimension execution satisfy all target/carrier dependencies; this is not just a poset cover.\n- Supplied-copy delivery tails: **85 H1 + 17 H2 + 19 H3 + 20 H4**, rank mass **256**, versus mass **440** for a reconstructed 55-chain best-global-order witness. The histogram improves componentwise; no global tail-moment optimum is claimed.\n- All target tails and all 416 scalar reads remain charged. Eight inherited rank-seven drops still cost COPY56.\n- All 32 injected dirty-copy contaminants have nonzero target responses, making the missing arbitrary-dirty formation/restoration contract explicit.\n\n## Scope and limitations\n\nThis is one pinned decoder's minimal-prefix, fixed-centre, no-redrop geometry. Exact centre values are supplied at singleton survivor frames, and every subsequent delivery/target frame move through the declared exits is counted. **Formation of 24 additional exact copies, arbitrary-dirty restoration, side corrections, hosting, precision, and all-size admission remain unresolved and are not free.** No physical supplier, original card's 5% gate, new kappa, or frontier update is claimed. #1125's retained-cost premise and two-extra-rank budget warning remain intact.\n\n## Evidence\n\nOnly `research/p104-target-order-delivery/` is added: proof/scope README, exact schedule and receipt, standalone verifier, TASK/SOURCES/VERIFY metadata, and complete selection JSON.\n\nActually exercised on **CPython 3.12.12**:\n\n```sh\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -O -B research/p104-target-order-delivery/verify.py\n# PASS_P104_TARGET_ORDER_DELIVERY chains=32 extra_arrays=24 reads=416 lower_bound=32 controls=8 no_new_kappa\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-target-order-delivery\n# PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/p104-target-order-delivery outcome=completed\n```\n\nThe parent independently replayed the registered package before publication. After final PR1125 attribution/pin changes, receipt generation and `--check-only` passed again. Positive controls reproduce the exact P104 decoder, eight single-cut chain counts of 19, and the 55-chain global-order witness. Eight semantic negative/limitation controls remain active under `-O`. OR-Tools was used only to discover the witness; replay is standard-library and exact. No full supplier cold replay, hosted CI, native compiler, or proof-assistant verification is claimed.\n\n## Provenance and credit\n\nIndependent round-two seed **4e1451a884a6979cb599a332ccc7ad40**, track **complex-mechanisms**, emitted card **complex-rank-shape-decoder**, exact baseline **0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea**. Scope explicitly changed from a complete block-decoder supplier to this missing attainment lemma. Final overlap corrected the initial failure to locate merged/local #1125; its theorem is credited and pinned, not republished as new.\n\nCredit Ali Romman/#1125; Josie Elliston/#1071; themilkman216/#968; DreamingOfClouds/#717/#446/#595; Joel Pulikkan/GamingPuzzled/#620; Douglas Colkitt/#1240 and the selected construction lineage. Prepared for Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex (gpt-6-astra) assistance; Apache-2.0.\n\nClaim/finding: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1929#discussioncomment-18925825\n",
